From c265ca2fc4b9b54ba75b6780e110c566483c93d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: build-engine <build-engine@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 11:49:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(drama3): reuse a voice reference's prefill across
 requests

Keep one live KV prefix and one reusable recurrent-state snapshot pair per
Metal lane. The prompt builder reports the invariant reference boundary;
cache identity includes the tower lookahead row and compares exact owned
frames rather than a hash alone. Preserve original prefill chunk cuts.

Invalidate before incompatible/default prefill and on execution failure.
Reuse GPU-owned buffers across voice switches, including partial-allocation
failures. Rebuild per-request decode counters and leave CUDA uncached.

Add deterministic boundary, exactness, invalidation, ownership and prompt
regressions. Corrects PR17's stale A/default/A state and per-switch leak.

Link the Metal/Objective-C frameworks for the macOS host-check target.
